  "kind": "building",
  "notes": "University (12×12): a closed quadrangle of warm stone around a cloister court — across the back the great hall with tall arched windows, buttresses and a bell tower with a clock, lantern and terracotta cupola at its centre; on the left the library wing (taller, buttressed, tall arched windows, dormers); on the right the colleges (stone ground floor, plastered upper floor, chimneys); along the road a lower front range with the gatehouse (arched passage, blue crest, pyramid roof, a blue banner, two round turrets). Inside, a columned cloister arcade under lean-to terracotta roofs surrounds four lawns, crossing paths, a fountain and four round trees (signature: cloister and bell tower).",
